WEBVTT

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:23.930
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:31.270
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:39.000
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:45.140
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.920
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:57.630
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:04.600
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:12.540
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:20.210
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.490
"Daiichi Central Hospital"

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:33.900
"Ken Nakajima"

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.460
It was a clean break, so
it'll heal pretty fast.

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:42.200
Don't be stupid. I was
worried about you.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:47.940
It's just like the Inspector said.
They're making fools of us.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:23.100
FILE. 42
ROUND IT GOES!
THE FIERY PATROL
LIGHT (PART 2)

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.890
What's their motive? What
are they doing this for?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.590
I don't know.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.390
If only we had
some clues.

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:55.610
"The 009 Task Force"

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:00.140
Inspector! We'll never catch them
if we hold back like this!

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.680
We'll just end up with more officers
down, like Nakajima.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:06.290
That's right! We must
avenge Nakajima.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.790
He's not dead.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.350
He's not dead.
Let us get revenge for Nakajima!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.000
I said, he's not dead!

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.020
I said, he's not dead!
Calm down. Please! We were...

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.690
We're not talking
about that!

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.400
I've come to
ask a favor.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:30.170
I want to get a change of clothes.
Do I have your permission?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:34.610
You came all this
way to ask that?

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.750
Then I have your
permission, sir?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.830
Officer Tsujimoto.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:43.790
Yes.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:48.190
Don't forget you're a cop, even
when out of uniform.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.860
You can go.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:58.370
Hello! It's been
a long time.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:02.900
How's the training
going?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.980
Hmm... So what's
on your mind?

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.780
Really? Yeah.
I know. I see.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.150
Thanks a lot.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:24.260
Tokuno? Can I speak
with you?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.770
A Special Traffic
Mobile Unit?

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:40.240
Many applications have been made,
but they keep getting rejected.

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:45.190
And Toukairin's telling you
to get the applications.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.120
He's been worried about our station,
so he's gone out on his own...

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:54.160
...getting information to help us. He's
the source of the frequency leak.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.800
Did you call for me?

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:02.500
Did you call for me?
I want you to do something... confidentially.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.190
Bokuto Station.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.630
What?

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.370
What's happened?

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.770
Nakajima's disappeared from the hospital.
What's happened?

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:38.840
Chief, are you certain about this?

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:41.680
Chief, are you certain about this?
Toukairin says it's possible.

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:46.250
But the Special Traffic Mobile
Unit was never formed.

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:49.010
It's just the ghost
of a unit.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:49.950
Here it is.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:55.760
"Applications forthe Special
Traffic Mobile Unit"

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:57.760
Look at this.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:58.930
Scroll down.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.260
Yes.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.770
The name of the applicant is Inspector
Kondo, of Headquarters.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:07.390
Also listed are the names of Detectives
Ikezawa and Oki. Three names in all.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:13.030
Since March of two years ago, there
has been a total of... 13!

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.740
Thirteen applications?!

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:16.880
Thirteen times
in two years.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.880
The elite of the traffic police have
wanted a Special Unit for years.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:26.120
The plan would permit the Unit to
respond to criminal activity...

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:31.180
...without regard to any
jurisdictional lines.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.030
It would be a dream come
true for them.

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:37.260
Their applications have
been ignored.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.270
They must have
snapped...

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:44.300
So that's why they've taken the matter
into their own hands?

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:46.770
And are acting so
recklessly?

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:53.280
Headquarters turned them down. They must
have known what these guys were like.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:54.280
It's ridiculous.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.250
It's ridiculous.
However, they underestimated Bokuto Station...

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:04.260
...and, in particular,
Nakajima.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:08.730
So they decided to
go after us.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.270
Although, this is just
a theory.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:16.470
We'll know when
we catch them.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:19.870
I'll report to the
Inspector.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:24.880
Miyuki! Uh... umm...
Nakajima's...

00:07:25.050 --> 00:08:07.990
What?

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.060
Yes. I understand.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:23.130
Tsujimoto's broken a wrist and dislocated
her shoulder. That seems to be it.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:28.370
But she is going in for a
MRI, just to be sure.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.970
We've got no time to
be feeling relief!

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:35.070
Apprehend those
outlaws. ASAP!

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:38.090
"New Health Insurance Card"

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.350
Natsumi!

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.590
How disgraceful.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:45.060
How disgraceful.
Cheer up.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:47.030
How's Nakajima?
Cheer up.

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.570
Oh.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:52.540
I'll take you home.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.210
Tsujimoto.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.340
Yes?

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.680
You're a good cop.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:01.710
I don't agree.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:06.650
Cops that think they're good, aren't.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:10.120
Like Inspector Kondo
and the others?

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.190
Let me tell you
something.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:16.390
Being a cop is nothing more
than being a public servant.

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:21.420
Do your
best.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.040
We cannot find Inspector
Kondo anywhere, sir.

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.780
He's disappeared.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.750
So what?

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:43.850
Inspector. I need 200 patrol cars.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.340
200?!

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:50.360
Don't be absurd. Do you know how many
patrol cars the city has?

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:58.460
801. 600 are available. I'm
asking for 1/3 of those.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:03.010
I want to chase them onto the Metropolitan
Highway, and then block all the ramps.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.940
It's a good plan, but you can't
have 200. You can have 150.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.680
I said 200, and that's what I need!

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:15.520
150! And that's final!

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:21.150
I've never rigged the rear brakes to
be hand-controlled before.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:22.660
It's a first, even for me.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:25.150
I really appreciate it, Dad.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:29.390
This business about cops committing
crimes is shameful.

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:32.130
What's this country
coming to?!

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:37.840
Dad! I'm proud
of being a cop.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:42.740
Anyway that's what law enforcement
is all about... providing security.

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:47.580
I can't let those renegades
remain at large!

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:51.590
There you are! I figured
you'd be here.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.760
Hello, stranger.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:57.090
Tsujimoto! What'd you do to your hand?!

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.820
I know. Now I won't be
able to ride my bike.

00:11:02.030 --> 00:11:03.860
Not alone,
anyway.

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:07.530
Daimaru, sorry, we won't need
your hand brake.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:11.300
I'm going to take the place
of your son's legs!

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.980
He's here. I'll pass
you to him.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.560
Hello?

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.180
I've been worried about you.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.750
Things have been so crazy with this case, I
haven't been able to get out of the station.

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:32.030
Sorry.

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:33.360
That's okay.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:36.020
The most important thing right
now is to catch those guys.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.730
We just got word that
they've been sighted.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:42.010
Really. Kobayakawa...

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.440
Yes?

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:45.940
Let's get together later.

00:11:45.940 --> 00:11:48.810
Okay.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:53.420
Well, I'm off.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:57.010
Ken. I'll disown you if you blow this.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:00.020
I'm counting on
you too, girl.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:04.520
300. I definitely need
300 cars, Director!

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.290
No. The best I
can do is 200.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.660
I'm pleading with
you! 300!

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.320
Listen, I'll get
you 250.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:14.370
But that's the best I can do.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.530
Thank you very much!

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:20.510
I'll be taking your car away
for a while for this.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:24.270
I'll buy a 3-month
train pass.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:31.010
You'll get a better deal if you
buy a 6-month pass.

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:36.290
It's stifling
out here.

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:46.790
Kondo, Ikezawa and Oki are on the
third street up, heading south.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:51.770
Bokuto Station shall put all efforts
into catching these guys.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.940
We're going to bend the
rules a little here.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:03.280
I don't care what you do, as long
as you don't use the radios!

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.250
This is an order
to all units.

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:10.550
There will be absolutely no
radio communication.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:15.100
Now move
it!

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:27.070
There they are.
Ready?

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.210
Ready!

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:35.210
"Tokyo Metropolis Highway 50m Ahead"

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:09.050
"Hakozaki Entrance Closed"

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:11.520
"Central Beltline Closed"

00:14:11.690 --> 00:14:18.190
"Closed"

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:29.330
60% of routes are blocked off. A
total of 250 cars are deployed.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:32.030
250?!

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:37.670
Just in, Kobayakawa and the Bokuto units
have just entered the downtown loop.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.420
Where are the bastards?

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.610
Just beyond Kiba, heading for Shiohama.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:46.880
Tsujimoto and Nakajima
are in pursuit.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:54.550
Blocking is not complete!
There're cars up ahead!

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:59.800
It's too late to worry about that. If we get
ahead of them all, we'll be all right.

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:08.240
"Emergency Telephone"

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:18.750
They are now heading south on Route
No. 9, and they've passed Shiohama.

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:21.560
Are they okay?

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.750
Are they okay?
Yes. It's confirmed.

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:28.490
How in the world are they steering
that thing, anyway?

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:31.200
They're heading for the Bayshore Route.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.840
They are?

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:37.740
Yeah. A favorite with speeders.

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.330
Those punks.

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:44.910
Kondo and his accomplices
are trying to rule the roads.

00:15:45.350 --> 00:15:49.410
They're complete
maniacs!

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:57.860
Miyuki!

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.130
Oh, no!

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.030
What?

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:02.660
I don't want her to see us riding like this.

00:16:02.830 --> 00:16:07.170
Don't be stupid! You sound
like you're 13!

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:18.110
They've just entered the Bayshore Route.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:20.640
Which way?

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.320
Toward Ariake Junction!

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:23.980
Oh.

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.520
Up ahead of them...

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:27.250
...is the Rainbow Bridge.

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:33.250
That's where it'll
go down.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:08.020
I'll make you stop! No
matter what it takes!

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.880
Oh. My poor car.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:20.180
Kobayakawa!

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:23.440
Here they come!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:37.290
Natsumi!

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:39.090
No! Stop this!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.800
You're supposed to be police officers!

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:42.700
Let's give it another shot, Nakajima.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:45.270
What are we going to do?
Let's give it another shot, Nakajima.

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:45.400
What are we going to do?

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:49.430
We're going to hit back at them!

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:54.840
I'll show them what happens when
they mess with Bokuto Station!

00:18:20.440 --> 00:18:22.630
Whoa!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.240
Loser!

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:27.330
Tsujimoto! Promise not to kick him, too!

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:30.370
Sandwich him...

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.720
What?

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:35.840
I... said... sandwich... him!

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:39.150
I get it. Let's stop
fooling around!

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.620
Gas it! We'll get him, no matter
how far he tries to run!

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:44.760
Yeah!

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:08.110
Oki and Ikezawa are being
taken to the hospital.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:14.350
Oki broke his shoulder. And Ikezawa has
broken his left leg. Nothing fatal.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:17.090
That leaves one
more to go.

00:19:17.190 --> 00:19:20.820
They stopped the bikes, but how
are they going to stop that car?

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:25.500
Surely Kondo wouldn't
slam into the barricade.

00:19:26.270 --> 00:19:30.430
Unless he's a Special
Traffic Kamikaze Unit.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:40.880
He's completely lost it. He's given
up everything that he was.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.150
There's a chance that he'll take a shot at it.

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:45.220
You can't be serious.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:48.160
Wait a minute!
You can't be serious.

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:52.590
Even if that's what he's trying to
do, we still have one trump card.

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:54.360
Huh?

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:57.360
The wisdom and courage of your officers.

00:19:59.370 --> 00:20:23.390
Here they come! It's
Nakajima's V Max!

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:24.390
Let's do it!

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:26.990
Okay!

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:43.040
I'm counting on
you, Tsujimoto.

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.150
I don't know why this guy
thinks he's so elite.

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:53.450
Playtime's over, buddy!

00:21:56.090 --> 00:22:02.290
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:12.200
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.800 --> 00:22:19.100
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:28.950
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:43.190
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:51.470
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.540 --> 00:23:00.050
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:08.120
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:17.660
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:18.070 --> 00:23:25.140
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:30.870
Ah! Chief!

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:37.110
What?! That photo can even be
seen in Rio de Janeiro?!

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:40.190
Yes! It's on
the Internet.

00:23:40.490 --> 00:23:44.690
Wow! I can't believe Nakajima's
doing stuff like that.

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:46.950
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 43...

00:23:47.230 --> 00:23:48.500
..."Bokuto Station Scandal."

00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:51.630
Ah! There's one of me!
